Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 6 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 three things sent back with R80a): THREE PROBES OF MAIN'S ARE MENDED, BESIDE
 THE FILES MAIN WROTE

Sent back with R80a (its note, section 4, items 2 to 4), and main's faults by main's word:
  - sm_rows_probe.py, main's recount of the SM seat's rows, gave another file on another machine. Three times
    were printed in the zone of the machine; and one row asked whether a commit is in the repository, which
    it is in main's alone, where it was a scratch commit on no branch. The file main kept gives that row as
    not held, against main's own table;
  - builder_rows_probe.py wrote its file and then ended in an error: its rows are numbers and texts, sorted
    together;
  - builder_rows_probe2.json is a kept output with no script.

The mend stands in the arc B1898, in verification/mended_in_r80b/, beside main's files as main wrote them
(verification/checks/), which the arc's lock holds by hash and which are not changed. It is the way main's
own corrected plant stands in verification/main_at_the_landing/.

  - the recount, mended: the times in UTC; the row asks whether the commit is on a branch or a tag. Run in
    two zones it gives one output: 15 rows, 15 held. Two rows differ from the file main kept, and one of
    them now agrees with main's table;
  - the first probe, mended in its last lines: it runs to its end. 33 cases, 29 made again;
  - the second probe, WRITTEN AGAIN by the builder from the fourteen lines main kept: one case for each
    line, given to the package's own function. Each of the fourteen gives the answer main kept. Where a line
    leaves the case open, the script says that the case is the builder's reading of it.

The two mended scripts are main's but for their marked blocks: each block gives the lines main wrote, and
with the blocks put back the file is main's byte for byte. The arc's lock holds that, and holds what the
kept runs say. It does not run the probes again: they answer for the package as it stood on the day, and a
series that mends a row changes its answer.

The arc's page has a dated note. Its lock passes: 9 tests. Every gate passes but the count of landings.
Main's faults by main's word; the cases of the second probe are the builder's and are not checked by main.
